The bowl holds about 20 dark, glossy oval pieces, most likely kalamata-type olives, with a few orange strands, possibly carrot or pepper. At roughly 4–5 g each, that comes to about 90 g of food.

Olives run about 150–230 kcal per 100 g depending on the type. With some oil on the surface, I'm using about 200 kcal per 100 g, which gives roughly 180 kcal.

